# Flutter Monorepo — Architecture & Imports

## Startup
Before writing any code, read:
- `AGENTS.md` — agent rules, package table, logging, error handling
- `DESIGN.md` — theming, spacing, typography, shared components

## Repo layout
```
apps/       ← app-specific wiring only (DI, flavors, assets)
packages/   ← all reusable logic; packages never depend on apps/
```

## Must-use packages

| Need | Package | Import |
|---|---|---|
| Logging | `logger` | `import 'package:logger/logger.dart';` |
| HTTP | `core` | `import 'package:core/core.dart';` |
| Error handling | `core` | `Result<T>`, `Success`, `Failure` |
| Local storage | `storage` | `import 'package:storage/storage.dart';` |
| Navigation | `routing` | `import 'package:routing/routing.dart';` |
| UI system | `design_system` | `import 'package:design_system/design_system.dart';` |

## Import rules
- Import only from the public barrel file: `package:foo/foo.dart`
- Never use deep-link imports: `package:foo/src/...`
- No cross-feature imports between features in the same app

## After pubspec changes
Always run `melos bootstrap`, never `flutter pub get` in a single package.

## Commits
Format: `type(scope): description`
Examples: `feat(core): add retry`, `fix(design_system): card radius`
